{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450525-non-tremere-apprentices","id":1450525,"title":"Non-Tremere Apprentices","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-31T18:21:19-07:00","id":1450525,"title":"Non-Tremere Apprentices","content":"This is something that is occasionally mentioned, and there's even a Ritual to &quot;awaken the potential for Thaumaturgy&quot; (even though as written, it doesn't really do anything), so I'm curious about the lore on this. If the Tremere came across a Caitiff with unusual powers, under what circumstances would they consider &quot;adopting&quot; them? How high a rank could they achieve? There's a situation in my current Chronicle where one of the Tremere players has befriended a Caitiff who was Embraced by a Giovanni and she wants to bring them into the Clan and House, and I can't decide if that's even a thing or not. This is a V20 question, but I am slowly bringing the Clan into a position more like in 5e, where the Pyramid becomes less monolithic, if that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T20:21:50-07:00","id":1450541,"title":"","content":"A branch of Indian tremere allowed other kindred to join in the hopes of gaining a foothold In hostile territory. They were known as trimira and were bloodbond to the inner council and not allowed to sire. Usually ravnos and nosferatu. <br /> <br /> If he has necromancy I'm sure a few tremere would be willing to work with him but he will likely end up bloodbonded and a slave teaching other tremere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T22:48:05-07:00","id":1450546,"title":"","content":"I'm <i>sure</i> I read something about this in something official, although it said that to get adopted by the pyramid you'll have to work your ass off, forswear loyalty to anything else and accept being second class to real Tremere. You will always be bottom of the barrel to them. (which makes sense). Hmm, I'll look for this when I have time today<br /> <br /> As a Giovanni, they'll have necromancy secrets to trade, but will very likely be marked for death and worse to follow by the family, who also expect total loyalty, and considered a spy by everyone else. But as a caitiff... <br /> <br /> <i>If the Tremere came across a Caitiff with unusual powers, under what circumstances would they consider &quot;adopting&quot; them? </i><br /> According to the sourcebook &quot;Outcasts&quot;, none. They would, however, be quite happy to use them in an experiment. <br /> <br /> <i>How high a rank could they achieve?</i><br /> Janitor? Slave? Comedic chantry mascot? The regent's new dartboard? A caitiff probably isn't getting inside the pyramid, ever, but if they're useful and not being dissected or such, they might get blood bonded and thrown scraps sometimes. <br /> <br /> I advise lying about their caitiff status, pass them off as a true necromancer<br /> <br /> There's also the Anarch Sorcerers, who will teach thaumaturgy without you needing to be Tremere, in a sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-01-2021, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T04:07:18-07:00","id":1450567,"title":"","content":"Well maybe a little more context. The Tremere PC was investigating the ruins of a mansion that had once belonged to a prominent family of mortal occultists. They found a secret chamber in what was once the house's basement, and there, they found a woman who had been staked, and the stake was magically warded. Upon freeing her, they found that she had been staked nearly a hundred years prior by a Giovanni who had fallen in love with her and made her a ghoul. Somehow she broke her Blood Bond and rejected the Giovanni, who, in anger, Embraced her, staked her, and killed her entire family. She wants revenge on the Giovanni as a result. As the woman knew nothing about Kindred society, the Apprentice got permission to train her by the Prince and her Regent, and discovered that the woman had some unique abilities (such as having developed an immunity to Ward versus Kindred and the ability to astrally project without the use of Auspex). Seeing the advantage of these abilities, the Apprentice's player is like &quot;Oh man we could totally train her to use Thaumaturgy and bring her into the Clan as a loyal ally&quot;. And I was like, with some other Clans you could do this, but the Tremere are....the Tremere. So I was just curious about the precedent before I make my ruling. It's my game, of course, I can do whatever I want, but I like to stay within the boundaries of the setting where I can- to me, the vast amount of vampire lore is a large part about what makes the game awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T08:58:42-07:00","id":1450589,"title":"","content":"Let me preface this with, your story, your world, your rules. What you say goes.<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;potential for Thaumaturgy&quot; in the sense that one kindred might be something akin to &quot;force sensitive&quot;. Its hedge magic/sorcery/liner magic and anyone can do it; human, vampire, werewolf, etc. What's special about Blood sorcery is it uses viate as a &quot;power source&quot;.<br /> <br /> If a caitiff was found with blood sorcery their might be a slim chance of induction if passed off as a wayward Tremere (similar to bloodlines maybe) but more than likely they would just be killed. Anyone else would be tortured to figure out how and where they learned the blood magic, then killed. Then the leak would be hunted down and tortured to figure out if it ends with them, then killed. If its a person that has blood magic they want they would welcome them in under false pretenses, bond them, learn everything they know, then they would be tortured to figure out what else they know, then killed.<br /> <br /> A regent would never allow an apprentice to teach blood magic to anyone outside the clan, both the person in question and the apprentice would be killed if they did (maybe even just for asking).<br /> <br /> Immunity to Ward versus Kindred and the ability to astral project without the use of Auspex pretty much guarantee this person is kept alive to figure out how any of that is possible.<br /> <br /> SO here is how I would play it: Apprentice asks, Prince and Regent say yes, this Giovanni gets brought in, blood bonded to the regent and put in well furnished prison cell in the chanty where they are the regents new project. The apprentice will forget about it and is basically grounded until they relearn the code of Tremere and if they fight at all or give any push back they will be killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6922,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","user":"Houston810","date":". 06-01-2021, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6922-houston810","name":"Houston810","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T09:46:32-07:00","id":1450599,"title":"","content":"Naturally, your own story takes precedent over lore, but as for the written if you want her to be useful to the clan and learn thaumaturgy there is content for that in V20.<br /> <br /> You can ally with the Tremere without joining the clan. According to <i>Rites of the Blood</i>:<br /> &quot;It is rare, but Clan Tremere will often approve the teaching of Thaumaturgy under the following conditions:<ul><li>Capturing or destroying a notorious enemy wanted by the Tremere.</li> <li>Earning a life boon from a high-ranking warlock.</li> <li>The recovery of valuable Thaumaturgy artifacts or notes</li> <li>Exceptional acts of loyalty that serve the Clan as a whole&quot;</li> </ul><br /> The chantry will submit a request to the supervising Lord, who will investigate the potential student for warning signs that they're a threat to the clan. If the student is found wanting, the Regent is punished for not being careful enough.<br /> <br /> &quot;A student must surrender five points of her blood to the local chantry, three of which will be filed with the office of the Lord. In addition, the student must sign a blood contract that expressly forbids the use of any Thaumaturgy against a Tremere in good standing.&quot;<br /> &quot;Rarely, the Pyramid will allow a Tremere to exchange information about blood magic, such as rituals, with non-Camarilla thaumaturges. Sometimes, ambitious Tremere will agree to work under the table with fellow thaumaturges and hope their fellow Tremere won\u2019t discover their secret.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just my opinion, but keeping to the lore, I don't see this getting approved unless she proves absolutely indispensible.<br /> A Caitiff has no allies or conflicting loyalties to begin with, so except for the damage done to your reputation, she should be safe. But associating with caitiff will be a mark against the chantry caught associating with her, it's obscene to vampires of good standing. Also I don't see the Giovanni being thrilled about her existence, this doesn't come across as an embrace approved by the <i>Anziani</i>, it does nothing to further the family or their goals and if her sire is alive he's possibly grounded right now on account of disrespecting his elders and might want to clean this little accident up.<br /> <br /> The Tremere may simply wash their hands of this. They don't need to risk their reputation while offending supersitious elders, their own higher ups and a necromancer and/or his clan just to teach some Giovanni's ignorant bastard their arts when they can just lock her in a room somewhere and take her apart to find out what makes that magical immunity tick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-01-2021, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T10:04:25-07:00","id":1450601,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your replies, I felt that this was the case, but I wanted to be able to present a cogent argument for why this wouldn't fly based on the lore. I'll compromise and say that the Regent will allow the Caitiff to be named a ward of the Tremere politically, but leave it at that. Maybe teach her some minor Thaumaturgy if she is willing to endure the Inherited Affinity Ritual and sign a Blood Contract so that what she learns can never be turned against the Clan and House. Most games I've played in have been fairly strict about what Tremere will or would not do, but I kept seeing the occasional reference to non-Tremere Apprentices so I figured I'd find out if that is a thing. Under the current form of the Pyramid, it seems the answer is &quot;not bloody likely&quot; and I'm ok with that. I'll tell my player if she wants more, she can become a Regent and found her own Chantry one night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T10:32:04-07:00","id":1450695,"title":"","content":"There are some degrees of &quot;inside&quot; for the Tremere. Gargoyles have become sort of insiders, to the point where Thaumaturgy skills can happen. There is also membership in House Tremere as opposed to Clan Tremere. They're supposed to be extinct I think, except for the Maison Liban. But there may well be some last mortal Tremere in deep hiding somewhere.<br /> <br /> The Tremere also take pride in a self-image as more modern and less hidebound than other clans. They could adjust policy on such matters if the higher.ups saw the advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T11:53:14-07:00","id":1450709,"title":"","content":"Going all the way back to 1e Chicago By Night, the Tremere Chantry was instructing the Caitiff Gordon Keaton in Thaumaturgy in exchange for certain services he would perform for them. They didn't do this because they were nice or liked Gordon, but because he was an amoral bastard who do anything to get more power. This gave them someone who could perform tasks they wanted done, but couldn't put their fingerprints on or need someone disposable to do them.<br /> <br /> So this is a very old concept in the game. There's no reason to believe this is unique about the Chicago Chantry although it is probably not typical. Maybe there is approval needed from the Lord or even Pontifex and explanation required as to how this serves the Pyramid.<br /> <br /> What I imagine is that the Tremere place severe limits on such pawns (and they should always be seen as pawns, never equals to any Tremere). There are probably all sorts of &quot;proprietary&quot; Thaumaturgy Tremere would never teach outsiders (like anything they created themselves like Path of Blood). Keep it to &quot;common&quot; Paths known well before the Tremere show up and are often considered iconic vampire powers that don't have Disciplines. I'd pick things like Movement of Mind, Lure of Flames, and Weather Control. Be even more strict on Rituals. Once someone knows something, it can be taught to others. So Tremere won't want to share anything really good - just some basic stuff they know is already out there and available.<br /> <br /> They will also want to dribble out such knowledge so their pawn keeps coming back to them and staying loyal. That limited stock of knowledge may be something they intend to slowly be taught over many years, even decades. They won't want to teach someone all at once because their leverage ends.<br /> <br /> And the chantry should always have some kind of plan, even if it is only general at this point, on how to use such a person. Gordon was an &quot;Anarch&quot; because of his Caitiff status, but had no principles at all. So he was obviously useful in providing Anarch gossip to the Tremere, and likely spreading disinformation among the Anarchs. And when the Tremere were ready, they were going to ask him do things. Maybe to other Anarchs, or against certain enemies in the Camarilla that would be blamed on the Anarchs. He also controlled a brothel and that might be useful in expanding Herd, or planting spies (Gordon had high levels of Dominate) in someone else's Herd. And he was skilled in Finance, so he could be useful doing something there that they didn't want trace backed to them. So think about how your Caitiff could likewise be useful.<br /> <br /> So personally I would allow it, but make it clear that this Catiff Giovanni is not a &quot;friend&quot; or &quot;ally&quot; or member of the Chantry. They are a valuable pawn and asset that can be cultivated and used, and when needed discarded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T00:52:08-07:00","id":1450788,"title":"","content":"i imagine a number of Baali are among the Tremere, something they gained for helping them in their early nights and selling out the Salubri.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T08:05:15-07:00","id":1450818,"title":"","content":"I mean the Tzimisce managed to slip an agent into Oliver Thrace's Hong Kong chantry, and despite how ruthless and paranoid he is, he never seemed to catch on- though he did sell the guy out to the Kuei-Jin in order to save his own skin anyways...lol. Really what I always love about White Wolf is how there are two Clan Tremeres. There is this monolithic Pyramid that has such absolute control of their members that they never go Anarch...except when they do (House Goratrix, House Carna). They have absolute control of Thaumaturgy...except when they don't (many, many, examples, my personal favorite being the original Clanbook Giovanni, where they were like, oh yeah, we totally steal magic from the Tremere). I'm reminded of Leia's quote from A New Hope: &quot;<span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The more you </span></span></span><b>tighten</b><span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> your grip, Tarkin, the more star systems will slip through your fingers.&quot; </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T08:59:05-07:00","id":1450827,"title":"","content":"House Carna is Camarilla. Ipssimus is the Anarch house (which is, y'know, nonsensical, because would people who hate the control of the cam agree to form a single house so they can all be controlled among the Anarchs? Tremere, make your schemes less obvious please)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T13:49:15-07:00","id":1450880,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, Mentor background and Clan Friendship merit are things that exist. And the people the Tremere embrace from probably move in somewhat overlapping circles to the ones the Giovanni embrace family from. Occult interest, weird digs and artifacts, etc. A hundred years ago, victorian secret societies as well. Fewer people in their social layers too.<br /> <br /> Could be some rejected suitor, relative, lover or friend from her breathing days have been embraced and moved some way up the pyramid in the last century.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T02:00:32-07:00","id":1450931,"title":"","content":"So the issue is that the Tremere, by their very nature, are the In-Group. <br /> <br /> Most modern occult groups are counter-culture based or are otherwise &quot;outsiders&quot;; Wicca, thelema, conspiracy theorists, Neo-pagans. That kinda stuff. Settite priests embrace from cult members, and Assamite sorcerers look for active occultists because their caste is laser focused on magic, and that's part of the reason why Assamite sorcerers are like 1/10th of the Assamites at best. Assamite sorcerers are small to a fault. <br /> <br /> Not the Tremere. Because for the Tremere, an occult background is a plus, not deciding factor. Their first priority is finding a good fit for the pyramid; someone who's both ambitious and obedient, who works well with others, and who they wouldn't mind living with for a few hundred years. As for magic, Talent is more important than experience; ANYONE can learn thaumaturgy, you're a spiritual cripple if you can't, but Intelligence and willpower, along with a studious disposition, determine if you can use it well. Most magic styles are niche, fringe belief systems that don't get along with one another, but the Hermetic paradigm is something that accepts everything to some extent, it's an unusual &quot;centrist&quot; paradigm that appeals to all with a great amount of compatibility. The Ideal Tremere isn't much different from the ideal of many other clans; having good overlap with Nosferatu, Malkavians, Ventrue and Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T02:05:41-07:00","id":1450932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450525-non-tremere-apprentices?p=1450827#post1450827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Carna is Camarilla. Ipssimus is the Anarch house (which is, y'know, nonsensical, because would people who hate the control of the cam agree to form a single house so they can all be controlled among the Anarchs? Tremere, make your schemes less obvious please)</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a Tremere Loyalist would think that a House must be made of slaves.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <b>There is already canonical examples of Caitiff being adopted by the Tremere and taught Thaumaturgy</b><br /> <br /> Gordon Keaton was taught the rudiments of Thaumaturgy by Nicolai in Chicago by Night Second Edition. My view on the subject is that Nicolai was using him as a catspaw, though, and never intended him to learn anything more than the basics but those basics made him a powerful force among the Anarchs. Also, I think Nicolai was able to get away with it as one of the most powerful Regents in the whole of the New World. Ironically, he was more likely to break the rules there than someone who had less history of being a fanatical Tremere stooge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2021, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T02:22:32-07:00","id":1450934,"title":"","content":"All Tremere defections are Tremere plots. There are n